From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 20:43:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add common ToolStripItem members

Add the frequently-referenced ToolStripItem surface that was missing - the
accessibility members (AccessibleName/Description/DefaultActionDescription/Role and
AccessibilityObject), placement (Anchor, Dock, Available), and state/flags
(CanSelect, IsDisposed, IsOnDropDown, IsOnOverflow, DoubleClickEnabled, AllowDrop,
and the protected-internal DismissWhenClicked/ShowKeyboardCues). Because they live
on the base they reach every item type (buttons, menu items, labels, separators,
the hosted text/combo boxes). IsDisposed is wired into Dispose; IsOnDropDown reads
the owning strip.

They compile and round-trip; the GTK strip drives visual placement, so Anchor/Dock
are stored settings rather than live layout inputs. Covered by
ToolStripItemMembersFunctionalTests. Full Forms suite green at 2518.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
